# Every blob in this repo is stored with LF. Check it out that way too.
#
# Without this, a clone under core.autocrlf=true gets a CRLF working tree, and
# two things break that pass in the LF checkout the vendoring tool writes:
#   - skill-content checks that anchor on section headings ((?m)^## Limitations$)
#     stop matching, because the line is "## Limitations\r"
#   - per-file content hashes of the adapted vendor tree differ per clone,
#     since CRLF conversion changes the bytes being hashed
* text=auto eol=lf
